            }
          ],
          "title": "Practice Hold with your machine",
          "slug": "practice-hold-with-your-machine",
          "order": 2,
          "legacy": {
            "assignId": 1053,
            "blockType": "Document"
          }
        },
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "Both the heel and toe of our socks are formed with short rows. <br>\r\n<img src=\"/challenge/images/v2/31/stocking/shortrow_examples.png\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<br>Hand knitter might shape the toes and heels using a series of increases and decreases. \r\n\r\nBUT knit this way on a flat bed knitting machine, you'd need to seam the edges to create the pocket shape.\r\n<img width=\"50%\" src=\"/challenge/images/v2/31/stocking/increase_decrease_practice.png\">\r\n\r\n<h3>The more common way to shape the heels and toes is to use short rows.</h3>",
              "legacyComponentId": 2877,
              "order": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "video",
              "vimeoId": "251895484",
              "title": null,
