        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "Socks don't take a lot of yardage.  If you are knitting on a standard gauge machine, a 100gram ball of yarn will easily knit a pair of socks.<br>A food or postal scale is a knitters best friend!<br>If you are worried about having enough to finish your second sock, divide the ball in half before you start knitting.  Use a food scale to weigh the balls you create and there will be no worry about running out.<br>If you've already knit one sock, you can weigh it and compare the weight of the remaining yarn to confirm you have enough.",
              "legacyComponentId": 2918,
              "order": 1
            }
          ],
          "title": "Do I have enough yarn?",
          "slug": "do-i-have-enough-yarn",
